  accent="#ffe000"
  title="Support"
  description="Help with Pop Drop, a calm merge-the-balls game for iPhone."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="lede">Something not working, or an idea for the game? Email <a href="mailto:baralrobin@gmail.com?subject=Pop%20Drop">baralrobin@gmail.com</a> and I'll get back to you.</p>
  <p>It helps to mention your iPhone model and iOS version.</p>

  <h2>How do I play?</h2>
  <p>Slide to aim, tap to drop. Two balls of the same size merge into a bigger one. The round ends when the play area fills up past the line.</p>

  <h2>Where are the settings?</h2>
  <p>Tap the pause button. Settings has the colour theme, light or dark appearance, sounds and haptics.</p>

  <h2>My score isn't on the leaderboard</h2>
  <p>Check that you're signed in to Game Center in your iPhone's Settings. Scores are posted when a round ends, including one you give up from the pause menu.</p>

  <h2>I reset my best score, but Game Center still shows it</h2>
  <p>Resetting in Settings clears the best score on your iPhone only. Game Center keeps its own record.</p>

  <h2>Will I lose my round if I close the app?</h2>
  <p>No. An unfinished round waits for you next time you open Pop Drop.</p>
</AppPage>
